      "text": "ap      = the reader of what a person types after the word \"dmap\" - it exists only so the six commands below can be added to it\nsub     = the rule that the person must type one command name: map, retext, undo, show, lines, or sync\nm       = the map command and what it accepts: the code file, --block, --within, --at, --text, and --tries, 8 by default    (cmd_map)\nr       = the retext command and what it accepts: the code file, the entry id, and --text    (cmd_retext)\nu       = the undo command, it accepts one thing: the code file    (cmd_undo)\ns       = the show command, it accepts one thing: the code file    (cmd_show)\nl       = the lines command, it accepts one thing: the code file    (cmd_lines)\ny       = the sync command and what it accepts: the code file, --old, and --tries, 4 by default    (cmd_sync)\na       = the typed command after ap reads it\n            the person types, for example: dmap show notes.py\n            a then remembers two things: the command name \"show\", and the code file notes.py\nrun     = the step that starts the right work for the command name inside a\n            \"show\" starts (cmd_show), \"map\" starts (cmd_map), and so on\n            the started work receives a, so it knows the code file and the options",
